{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Cities of the kingdom of Og in Bashan. For only Og king of Bashan remained.</b> The reason Og ruled in that region is that he alone survived of the remnant of the Rephaim: from the war of Amraphel and his allies, who defeated the Rephaim at Ashteroth-karnaim (Genesis 14:5), many Rephaim remained, and those survivors the Ammonites defeated, as explained above (Deuteronomy 2:21), and from that war with the Ammonites he alone survived. And since he was mighty with the might of the rest of the Rephaim, therefore he became king."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:18.036664374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}